packages/admin/evolve_admin.egg-info/
# .claude/ is mostly local state, EXCEPT for project-level dev guardrails:
# pre-PR review hook, Stop adversarial verifier, worktree GC, the
# settings.json that wires them up, the META coordinator launcher skills
# (/meta /status /close), and the per-project substrate config meta.json
# (the repo slug the META flows resolve — see docs/spec-substrate-2026-06-15.md §16)
# so the system is reproducible from a clone. Per-user permissions stay in
# settings.local.json which is ignored below.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/meta.json
.claude/settings.local.json
postmortem-*.tar.gz
postmortem-*-extracted/
# Per-install ETR topology, generated by tools/etr-setup
docs/verification/rig-config.yaml
# Local-only docs (pod-specific incidents, diagnoses with billing detail or
# verbatim transcripts) — staged here for migration to a private companion
# repo. Lives on disk for the maintainer's reference; not shipped publicly.
docs/private/
# Machine-filed incident records from repo_puller versions that wrote into
# the deploy checkout (now write to {shared_dir}/repo-puller/incidents/).
# Ignoring the legacy path keeps stragglers from cluttering `git status` on
# the deploy box; nothing is ever committed here — curated records live in
# docs/incidents/.
issues/open/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
# EDR dispatch worktrees (edr.bridge.dispatch WORKTREES_SUBDIR) — local
# session isolation only; retained for post-mortem, never committed.
.edr/
# Stray test-artifact dir: a test that patches pwd.getpwnam with a MagicMock
# and then does Path(mock.pw_dir).mkdir(...) writes under the literal
# "MagicMock/getpwnam().pw_dir/..." path in the repo root. Ignore so a stray
# write can never be committed again.
MagicMock/
